{"step_index":429,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:47:45Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-07T07:47:45+01:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-07T07:47:45+01:00\nShowing lines 195-226 of 226\n195:    - Moves the hostile executable to `.quarantine/` with an appended `.quarantine` extension.\n196:    - Removes write and execution permissions from the file.\n197: 4. **Phase 4: Audit Trail:**\n198:    - Logs timestamp, target PID, binary path, SHA-256, and outcome to `database/incident_audit.json`.\n199: \n200: ---\n201: \n202: ## 9. SMTP Email Alerts & Reports (`backend/email_notifier.py`)\n203: \n204: ### 9.1 Report Generation\n205: `EmailNotifier.generate_html_report(data)` compiles a responsive, dark-themed HTML email containing:\n206: - Executive Summary Badge (System Health Index, Active Threat Count).\n207: - Detailed Threat Remediation Table (Process Name, PID, File Path, Threat Score, Heuristic Triggers).\n208: - Remote Desktop & RMM Tool Inventory.\n209: - High-Risk Network Sockets and Remote Endpoints.\n210: - Remediation Audit History.\n211: \n212: ### 9.2 Dispatch Pipeline\n213: - Connects securely via `smtplib.SMTP(host, port)`.\n214: - Upgrades to TLS encryption with `server.starttls()`.\n215: - Authenticates using credentials from `database/email_config.json`.\n216: - Sends MIME multipart message (`text/plain` fallback and `text/html`).\n217: \n218: ---\n219: \n220: ## 10. Threat Simulation Lab (`backend/simulator.py`)\n221: \n222: Allows operators and evaluators to safely test AegisShield's detection, alerting, and eradication capabilities without downloading malicious files:\n223: 1. **`temp_trojan`:** Drops and launches a harmless Python sleep process inside `%TEMP%` named `svch0st_sim.exe`.\n224: 2. **`encoded_cmdline`:** Spawns a background process with `-enc` and `-w hidden` parameters.\n225: 3. **`rmm_beacon`:** Spawns a benign local loopback listener on port `5900` mimicking a VNC server.\n226: "}
{"step_index":430,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:47:45Z","input_tokens":2844,"cache_read_tokens":85000,"output_tokens":1090,"tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\thann\\\\Downloads\\\\AntiGravity\\\\SpywareProcessMon\\\\docs\\\\CODE_EXPLANATION.md\"","Replacement":"\"## 10. Threat Simulation Lab (`backend/simulator.py`)\\n\\nAllows operators and evaluators to safely test AegisShield's detection, alerting, and eradication capabilities without downloading malicious files:\\n1. **`temp_trojan`:** Drops and launches a harmless Python sleep process inside `%TEMP%` named `svch0st_sim.exe`.\\n2. **`encoded_cmdline`:** Spawns a background process with `-enc` and `-w hidden` parameters.\\n3. **`rmm_beacon`:** Spawns a benign local loopback listener on port `5900` mimicking a VNC server.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Master Diagnostic & Testing Engine (`tools/test_engine.py`)\\n\\n### 11.1 TestRunner Architecture\\nThe `TestRunner` class provides an isolated, assertions-based verification harness executing sequential unit, integration, and E2E checks:\\n- Tracks total passed and failed checks.\\n- Formats terminal output with ANSI color codes (`\\\\033[92m` for PASS, `\\\\033[91m` for FAIL).\\n- Exits with returncode `0` on 100% pass, or `1` on any failure for CI/CD integration.\\n\\n### 11.2 The 9 Diagnostic Suites\\n1. **Threat Detection & Heuristics:** Enumerates running processes and evaluates masquerading rules.\\n2. **Process Eradication:** Spawns a simulated threat and executes forced kernel-level termination, verifying PID cleanup.\\n3. **Access Control Policy:** Adds and tests Allowlist (whitelist) and Blocklist (blacklist) rules, verifying in-memory set matching and persistent cleanup.\\n4. **Network Origin Tracer:** Validates RFC 1918 private LAN classification and verified Cloud CDN classification (Google DNS `8.8.8.8`).\\n5. **AdBlock Rules:** Evaluates commercial ad domains (`adservice.google.com`, `ad.doubleclick.net`, `criteo.com`) and clean domains (`github.com`).\\n6. **Intercepting Proxy Socket Test:** Starts `AdBlockProxyServer` on `127.0.0.1:8080`, probes listener socket, and checks domain interception.\\n7. **Web Traffic Logging & Analytics:** Simulates request logging, timestamp recording, and verifies analytics metrics calculation.\\n8. **Email Report Generation:** Validates HTML compilation and pr\n<truncated 1400 bytes>","Target":"\"## 10. Threat Simulation Lab (`backend/simulator.py`)\\n\\nAllows operators and evaluators to safely test AegisShield's detection, alerting, and eradication capabilities without downloading malicious files:\\n1. **`temp_trojan`:** Drops and launches a harmless Python sleep process inside `%TEMP%` named `svch0st_sim.exe`.\\n2. **`encoded_cmdline`:** Spawns a background process with `-enc` and `-w hidden` parameters.\\n3. **`rmm_beacon`:** Spawns a benign local loopback listener on port `5900` mimicking a VNC server.\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
