{"step_index":474,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:50:30Z","input_tokens":3412,"cache_read_tokens":102256,"output_tokens":1399,"thinking":"Considering the request to add a private mode feature, the existing directive to update and append all files including design and architecture necessitates an update to the project's structure. This addition will affect the codebase's existing architecture, requiring careful consideration of how to integrate the feature seamlessly. The implications for the testing engine are also being considered to ensure proper functionality of the new feature.\n\n\nDefining \"Private Mode\" functionality requires a systematic approach. Initial focus is on minimizing the disk footprint of browsing data by preventing logging of visited domains and URLs. Implementing masked telemetry is also crucial; obscuring user accounts, private paths, and local IPs within displays and reports enhances stealth.\n\n\nA \"Stealth Wipe\" functionality is being added to instantly clear browsing data; this includes cache directives, log purging, and cache flushing. The UI will feature an ON/OFF toggle in the dashboard, with a visible indicator reflecting the private mode's status.\n\nThe configuration file will need to include a `PRIVATE_MODE_ENABLED` setting. The web traffic logger will need logic for completely skipping disk logging or using in-memory only data, along with toggle and purge functions. The adblock proxy will inject privacy headers and suppress IP recording when active. The network tracer requires an update to skip external GeoIP queries when private mode is engaged.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"100","Path":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\thann\\\\Downloads\\\\AntiGravity\\\\SpywareProcessMon\\\\backend\\\\web_traffic_logger.py\"","StartLine":"1"}}]}
{"step_index":475,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:50:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-07T07:50:44+01:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-07T07:50:44+01:00\nShowing lines 1-100 of 127\n1: \"\"\"\n2: AegisShield - Web Traffic Logger\n3: Thread-safe persistent recording of every website browsed, timestamps,\n4: ad-blocking decisions, and data transfer volumes.\n5: \"\"\"\n6: \n7: import os\n8: import json\n9: import time\n10: import threading\n11: from datetime import datetime\n12: from pathlib import Path\n13: from typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional\n14: \n15: from .config import DATABASE_DIR\n16: \n17: TRAFFIC_LOG_FILE = DATABASE_DIR / \"web_traffic_logs.json\"\n18: \n19: \n20: class WebTrafficLogger:\n21:     \"\"\"Records and queries all intercepted HTTP/HTTPS web traffic.\"\"\"\n22: \n23:     _instance = None\n24:     _lock = threading.Lock()\n25: \n26:     def __new__(cls):\n27:         with cls._lock:\n28:             if cls._instance is None:\n29:                 cls._instance = super(WebTrafficLogger, cls).__new__(cls)\n30:                 cls._instance._init_logger()\n31:             return cls._instance\n32: \n33:     def _init_logger(self):\n34:         self.logs: List[Dict[str, Any]] = self._load_logs()\n35:         self._flush_lock = threading.Lock()\n36:         self._pending_writes = 0\n37: \n38:     def _load_logs(self) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n39:         \"\"\"Load traffic logs from disk.\"\"\"\n40:         if TRAFFIC_LOG_FILE.exists():\n41:             try:\n42:                 with open(TRAFFIC_LOG_FILE, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n43:                     return json.load(f)\n44:             except Exception:\n45:                 return []\n46:         return []\n47: \n48:     def _save_logs(self):\n49:         \"\"\"Persist logs to disk.\"\"\"\n50:         try:\n51:             with open(TRAFFIC_LOG_FILE, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n52:                 json.dump(self.logs[:3000], f, indent=2)  # Keep latest 3000 requests\n53:         except Exception:\n54:             pass\n55: \n56:     def log_request(\n57:         self,\n58:         domain: str,\n59:         method: str,\n60:         port: int,\n61:         is_blocked: bool,\n62:         category: str,\n63:         reason: str,\n64:         bytes_transferred: int = 0,\n65:         client_ip: str = \"127.0.0.1\"\n66:     ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n67:         \"\"\"Record an intercepted web browsing event.\"\"\"\n68:         now = datetime.now()\n69:         entry = {\n70:             \"id\": f\"req_{int(time.time() * 1000)}_{len(self.logs)}\",\n71:             \"timestamp\": now.isoformat(),\n72:             \"date_time\": now.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"),\n73:             \"domain\": domain.lower().split(\":\")[0].strip(),\n74:             \"method\": method.upper(),\n75:             \"port\": port,\n76:             \"status\": \"BLOCKED\" if is_blocked else \"ALLOWED\",\n77:             \"is_blocked\": is_blocked,\n78:             \"category\": category,\n79:             \"reason\": reason,\n80:             \"bytes_transferred\": bytes_transferred,\n81:             \"client_ip\": client_ip\n82:         }\n83: \n84:         with self._flush_lock:\n85:             self.logs.insert(0, entry)\n86:             if len(self.logs) > 3000:\n87:                 self.logs = self.logs[:3000]\n88:             self._pending_writes += 1\n89: \n90:             # Flush to disk every 5 requests or on blocked ads\n91:             if is_blocked or self._pending_writes >= 5:\n92:                 self._save_logs()\n93:                 self._pending_writes = 0\n94: \n95:         return entry\n96: \n97:     def get_logs(\n98:         self,\n99:         limit: int = 150,\n100:         status_filter: Optional[str] = None,"}
